## Checklist for New Providers

Before submitting a new provider, verify:

- [ ] Inherits from `LLMProvider`
- [ ] Implements `generate_response(prompt: str) -> str`
- [ ] Validates API key in `__init__`
- [ ] Uses httpx.Client with 30s timeout
- [ ] Includes all type hints
- [ ] Includes docstrings on class and methods
- [ ] Uses try/except for error handling
- [ ] Registered in `providers/factory.py`
- [ ] Exported in `providers/__init__.py`
- [ ] Added to `.env.example`
- [ ] Tested manually with API key
- [ ] Follows naming conventions (snake_case file, PascalCase class)
- [ ] No hardcoded secrets
- [ ] No use of async/await

## Summary

Implementing a new provider requires:
1. Create provider file inheriting from `LLMProvider`
2. Implement `generate_response` with httpx
3. Validate API key in `__init__`
4. Register in factory dictionary
5. Export in `__init__.py`
6. Update `.env.example`
7. Test manually

Always refer to @providers/openai_provider.py as the canonical example.
